    "body": "Which thread/process/whatever are these algorithms happening in?\n\nIt would be clearer, I think, if the thing that uses outside settings were hoisted out of the \"in parallel\" steps, when the object that it's supposed to poke at is clearly available.  Having a boolean that then gets used in the async steps is a lot clearer than the implicit \"yeah, do it here, except you can also do it earlier because the state is immutable\" thing we have going on here.\n",
